I take the raincoat bag.
I start to leave the shop.
Just then, I see a beautiful shirt.
It is a cotton shirt.
It has a nice pattern on it.
It is very hot and humid today.
I am feeling very tired now.
I ask, "Brother, how much is this shirt?"
He says, "Madam, it is for five hundred rupees."
The shirt seems fine to me.
Therefore, I don't try it on there.
I give him five hundred rupees.
He gives me the shirt and a paper receipt.
I carefully keep that receipt in my purse.
Now I want to go straight to my flat.
I come out of the shop.
I catch a bus to go home.
